Note (7): When sigma2 ({sigma}_gas_) is noted it is derived directly from
    the FWHM of the HI line.
Note (8): This is the distance from the Local Group surface defined in
    Section 3.1, while DMW and DM31 are from the center of the MW and M31.
    The DLGh value is the variation on the distance from this surface when
    the Milky Way mass is higher and the M31 mass is lower. The DLGl value
    is when the Milky Way mass is lower and the M31 mass is higher. The
    total Local Group mass remains the same in all cases.
Note (9): Lv, rh and sigma references as follows:
     5 = McConnachie (2012, J/AJ/144/4);
     6 = Simon (2019ARA&A..57..375S);
     7 = {sigma} is from Martin et al. (2016, J/MNRAS/458/L59);
     8 = Properties are from Drlica-Wagner et al. (2016ApJ...833L...5D);
     9 = {sigma} is from Carlin & Sand (2018ApJ...865....7C). No rh is given
          since this galaxy is highly disrupted;
    10 = {sigma} is from Simon et al. (2020, J/ApJ/892/137);
    11 = rh is from Bothun & Thompson (1988AJ.....96..877B);
    12 = The LMC has a very large stellar rotation component compared to the
          stellar dispersion component. Using the stellar dispersion value
          (20.2km/s), would lead to a severe underestimate of the total
          mass, so we use the gas dispersion calculated from the FWHM of the
          HI line;
    13 = Properties are from Homma et al. (2016ApJ...832...21H);
    14 = Properties are from Torrealba et al. (2019MNRAS.488.2743T);
    15 = Properties are from Homma et al. (2018PASJ...70S..18H);
    16 = {sigma}_*_ is from Kacharov et al. (2017, J/MNRAS/466/2006);
    17 = {sigma}_*_ is from Martin et al. (2014ApJ...793L..14M);
    18 = {sigma}_*_ is from Namumba et al. (2019MNRAS.490.3365N);
    19 = rh is from Martin et al. (2016ApJ...824L...5M). {sigma}_*_ is from
          Collins et al. (2020, J/MNRAS/491/3496);
    20 = {sigma}_*_ is from Taibi et al. (2020, J/A+A/635/A152);
    21 = {sigma}_*_ is from Sand et al. (2015ApJ...812L..13S);
    22 = {sigma}_*_ is from Barnes et al. (2001MNRAS.322..486B);
    23 = {sigma}_*_ is from Namumba et al. (2018MNRAS.478..487N);
    24 = {sigma}_*_ is from Bernstein-Cooper et al. (2014AJ....148...35B).
          rh in this case is the semi-major axis noted by
          McQuinn+ (2015, J/ApJ/812/158);
    25 = {sigma}_*_ is from Begum et al. (2005A&A...433L...1B);
    26 = {sigma}_*_ is from Bouchard et al. (2005AJ....130.2058B) and is
          consistent with the detection at the lower velocity by
          Koribalski+ (2018, J/MNRAS/478/1611);
    27 = {sigma}_*_ is from Koribalski et al. (2018MNRAS.478.1611K).
